== Rolling stock ==

=== Current ===
* '''5000 series''' (Type B, 8-car, 2018–present) — Manufactured by [[Okami Heavy Industries]], the 5000 series is the current rolling stock on the Asahi Line. Introduced in 2018, these trains feature modern passenger amenities including air conditioning, accessibility features, and real-time passenger information displays. The 8-car formations provide high capacity for the line's busy commuter traffic.

=== Retired ===
* '''1000 series''' (legacy) — The original rolling stock used on the Asahi Line since its opening in 1965. The 1000 series trains were gradually retired and fully replaced by the 5000 series in 2018. These trains served the line for over five decades and were a familiar sight on the eastern corridors of Okami. The 1000 series underwent several refurbishment programmes throughout its service life, including updates to interior fittings and propulsion systems, but was ultimately retired due to its age and the need for higher capacity and modern accessibility features.

